  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Panjpar. 2 players, 52 cards. 5 each, turn-up trump. Attack: 1/3/5 (3=pair+1, 5=two pairs+1). Beat with higher same suit or trump. Pick up = attacker attacks again. Draw to 5. Cannot attack with more than defender holds. First out wins.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Panjpar. Guess trump colour; correct guesser attacks first. Attack with 1, 3, or 5 cards. Defender beats or picks up. Draw to 5. First to empty hand wins.',
    objective: 'Empty your hand before your opponent. The player left with cards when the other goes out loses.',
    gameplay: '1. **Attack**: Play 1, 3, or 5 cards. 1 = any card. 3 = pair + third (e.g. 7-7-9). 5 = two pairs + fifth (e.g. K-K-4-4-7). 2. **Defend**: Beat each attack card with a higher same-suit card, or any trump on non-trump. Trump beats trump only with higher trump. 3. **Result**: Beat all â†’ defender attacks next. Unbeaten â†’ defender picks up those cards; attacker attacks again. 4. **Draw**: After each battle, both draw to 5 from stock (attacker first). 5. **Endgame**: When stock empty, no draws. Cannot attack with more cards than opponent holds. First to empty hand wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Beat with higher same suit, or any trump on non-trump; higher trump on trump.',
      'Defender may choose to pick up any cards instead of beating.',
      'Cannot attack with more cards than opponent has.',
      'Trump indicator stays in place until stock drawn; no exchange for low trump (unlike Durak).',
      'Draw can end in tie if both empty in final battle.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two players. A standard 52-card pack is used; each player receives five cards. The next card is turned face up for trump and the remainder form the stock. Before the deal, one player guesses the trump colour; the correct guesser attacks first.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack. Rank A (high) to 2 (low).',
      equipment: 'Standard deck.',
      dealing: 'Five cards to each player. Next card turned face up = trump. Remainder stacked face down on trump card (trump visible) = stock. Before deal, one player guesses trump colour; correct guesser attacks first.',
